<!-- cell: markdown id="1395a7f0-9154-4766-8333-681a0e2fe965" -->

# Captain Varn and her daughter

## High-level plot

1. Captain Varn leaves her daughter on Earth to command the corvette that escorts the mission to Mars.

2. At Mars, Varn and her daughter keep talking, and Varn tells her of her doubts about the excavation.

3. When the alien fleet arrives, Varn fears it will go on to Earth.

4. Varn believes her daughter will have no chance unless someone stands in the fleet's way. She says goodbye to her daughter, puts her corvette in the fleet's path, and dies.

## Low-level plot

Captain Varn watches the news with her daughter: a probe has found something under the surface of Mars.

Varn is given command of the corvette that will escort the mission to Mars, and tells her daughter she has to leave.

Varn says goodbye to her daughter and promises to talk to her every day.

Varn's corvette arrives at Mars with the laboratory ship, as the first samples come up from the excavation.

Varn calls her daughter. Her daughter says she misses her, and Varn says she misses her too.

Varn watches the excavators dig deeper, and tells her daughter that no one knows what the object is, yet the digging goes on.

Varn's daughter asks whether the object is dangerous, and Varn tells her not to worry.

Varn sees alien ships appear on her corvette's screens, far out around Mars.

Varn is ordered to protect the discovery, and knows her one weakly armed corvette cannot stop a fleet.

Varn hails the alien ships again and again, and gets no answer.

Varn asks the scientists on the laboratory ship what the aliens want, and they cannot tell her.

Varn tells her daughter about the ships, and that she is afraid they will go on to Earth.

Varn believes that unless someone stands in the fleet's way, her daughter will have no chance on Earth. She sends her daughter a last message to say goodbye.

Varn moves her corvette into the fleet's path to buy her daughter time.

The fleet fires, and Varn's corvette is destroyed.

Varn's daughter receives her mother's last message.

<!-- cell: note id="dca7728d-3313-43e2-9dc1-2878b99cc3c0" -->

## Captain Varn and her daughter

How Captain Varn gave her life to buy her daughter time.

1. Captain Varn leaves her daughter on Earth to command the corvette that escorts the mission to Mars.
2. At Mars, Varn and her daughter keep talking, and Varn tells her of her doubts about the excavation.
3. When the alien fleet arrives, Varn fears it will go on to Earth.
4. Varn believes her daughter will have no chance unless someone stands in the fleet's way. She says goodbye to her daughter, puts her corvette in the fleet's path, and dies.

